1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
▸ VERA — every rupee traceable, audited before it moves.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
▸ Live platform stats lead into the core idea: the 9-stage verifiable fund trail.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
▸ Two modules, one standard of proof — VERA Core on Ethereum escrow, Hisaab of the Road on Solana.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
▸ A public trust network — campaigns register on-chain and every release is created against proof.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000
▸ Featured verified campaigns — live on-chain status, funding progress and audit access.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,000
▸ NGO trust scoring is deterministic — a transparent 100-point formula, not star reviews.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
STEP 0 · SIGN IN
One account for the citizen portal, org hub, contractor desk and auditor workspace.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
STEP 1 · BIND A WALLET
MetaMask signs a one-time message to unlock real on-chain value.

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,000
STEP 2 · DONATE
Pick an amount and confirm with the wallet — the donation lands on-chain.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,000
▸ Donation confirmed & earmarked — reference ID issued, ring-fenced, locked in escrow.

11
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000
▸ Dashboard update: ₹1,000 donated, one active escrow. "Trace" opens the full journey.

12
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
▸ Receipt — Confirmed → Earmarked → Locked in Escrow. Released only against verified milestones.

13
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,000
▸ The audit timeline — every event carries its actor and timestamp.

14
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,000
STEP 3 · REPORT A POTHOLE
A photo becomes public evidence in under a minute.

15
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:20,000
▸ Capture photo, GPS and description — then Gemini analyzes severity, size and surface type.

16
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:25,000
▸ Verdict: HIGH severity · 85 cm · asphalt · 95% confidence. Three citizen confirmations required to fund.

17
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:30,000
▸ Street Register — the public ledger of road defects: open, in repair, escrowed, fully paid.

18
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:35,000
▸ Anyone can confirm a pothole — three independent confirmations lock money into escrow.

19
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,000
▸ Organizations — every campaign runs through a verified NGO with a public audit trail.

20
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:50,000
▸ Campaign audit timeline — created, activated, funded, escrowed. Actors and timestamps throughout.

21
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:55,000
▸ On-chain block explorer — donation created → confirmed → locked, every block hash-anchored.

22
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:05,000
▸ Every rupee passes a 9-stage pipeline: milestone capping → evidence → AI verification → auditor sign-off → 2-of-3 multisig → blockchain release.

23
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:10,000
▸ Admin console — Hisaab operations: complaints, escrows, fund requests and contractors at a glance.

24
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:15,000
▸ Inspecting a complaint — the Gemini verdict, citizen confirmations and the trust model.

25
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:25,000
▸ Complaint queue — confirm → attach a government fund request → assign a contractor → the escrow locks.

26
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:30,000
▸ Fund requests — apply to government repair budgets; once sanctioned, they can back an escrow.

27
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:35,000
▸ Verification gates: organizations must be VERIFIED before raising campaigns; auditors are invite-only.

28
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:40,000
▸ Login audit — every sign-in attempt across web console and mobile API is recorded.

29
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:45,000
▸ Auditor workspace — independent review of milestone evidence. Queue currently clear.

30
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:55,000
▸ Switching to the organization portal — the NGO's workspace for campaigns, milestones and proofs.

31
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:10,000
STEP 4 · DEFINE MILESTONES
Each phase gets an allocated amount and verification criteria. Money releases per milestone — never as a lump.

32
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:20,000
STEP 5 · SUBMIT PROOF
Claimed utilization plus invoices — AI OCR cross-checks and flags discrepancies (₹0 here).

33
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:35,000
▸ Proof submitted — milestone now under review; every file is SHA-256 hashed into the immutable audit trail.

34
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:40,000
STEP 6 · CREATE CAMPAIGN
Title, funding goal, beneficiary and milestone plan — publish as active.

35
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:48,000
▸ Finally, the contractor desk — jobs assigned by the admin, paid in stages from on-chain escrow.

36
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:56,100
▸ Payout rules: stage 1 (~40%) releases on AI verification pass; the rest after the 30-day durability hold — after-photo + drive-over roughness score.
